flowchart TD
  accTitle: Worker runtime guardrail flow
  accDescr {
    The diagram shows the backend installing the worker runtime in shadow mode, validating
    manifests, restricting scoped Worker DB commands, and only allowing production actions
    after cutover gates are met. If the gates are not met, production writes stay off and
    legacy ingestion remains the owner.
  }
  A[Backend enables worker runtime framework] --> B[Shadow mode default with production writes disabled]
  B --> C[Service manifests validated by runtime manager]
  C --> D[Scoped Worker DB commands allowed only on /api/worker/db/*]
  D --> E[Shadow commands record receipts and avoid live publication]
  C --> F{Cutover gates met?}
  F -- No --> G[Keep production writes off and legacy ingestion as owner]
  F -- Yes --> H[Production scoped commands can proceed with guards]
  H --> I[Operators use protected workflow actions for deploy, restart, recovery]
